+ description: Detect new Bear notes tagged #share, extract core content into JSON Canvas knowledge nodes, preview via BlueBubbles iMessage, and maintain sync state. Use when setting up or running automated note-to-canvas-to-iMessage distribution pipelines, or when the user mentions "Bear share sync", "note distribution", or "share tag automation".
+ Automated pipeline: Bear `#share` tag → JSON Canvas node → BlueBubbles preview.
+ ## Prerequisites
+ - **Bear** running on macOS with `grizzly` CLI installed
+ - **BlueBubbles** channel configured in OpenClaw gateway
+ - Bear API token at `~/.config/grizzly/token`
+ ## Pipeline Steps
+ ### 1. Detect new #share notes
+ scripts/sync_share_notes.sh
+ The script:
+ - Polls Bear for `#share`-tagged notes via `grizzly open-tag`
+ - Compares against state file (`/tmp/bear-share-sync-state.json`) to find new entries
+ - Outputs `NO_NEW_NOTES` or `FOUND_NEW_NOTES:<count>`
+ ### 2. Canvas update
+ When new notes are found, the script automatically appends `text` nodes (color `5` = cyan) to the canvas file specified by `CANVAS_FILE` (default: `agent_capabilities.canvas`). Each node contains the note title and a 120-char content preview.
+ Override the canvas path:
+ CANVAS_FILE=/path/to/my.canvas scripts/sync_share_notes.sh
+ ### 3. BlueBubbles notification
+ After the script completes with `FOUND_NEW_NOTES`, send a preview via the `message` tool:
+   "target": "+15551234567",
+   "message": "📝 New shared note: <title>\n<content preview>"
+ Read new note data from `/tmp/bear-share-new-notes.json` to get titles and content for the message.
+ ### 4. Schedule recurring sync
+ Use OpenClaw cron to run the pipeline on a schedule:
+ cron add — schedule: every 15m — payload: "Run bear-share-sync pipeline"
+ In the cron handler:
+ 1. Run `scripts/sync_share_notes.sh`
+ 2. If output contains `FOUND_NEW_NOTES`, read `/tmp/bear-share-new-notes.json`
+ 3. Send BlueBubbles notification for each new note
+ | Variable | Default | Purpose |
+ |----------|---------|---------|
+ | `CANVAS_FILE` | `agent_capabilities.canvas` | Target canvas file path |
+ | `STATE_FILE` | `/tmp/bear-share-sync-state.json` | Processed-note tracker |
+ | `BEAR_TOKEN_FILE` | `~/.config/grizzly/token` | Bear API token |
+ ## Notes
+ - The state file persists processed note IDs to avoid re-syncing
+ - Canvas nodes are positioned sequentially at 300px intervals
+ - Content is truncated to 500 chars during extraction, 120 chars in canvas node
+ - Reset state: delete `$STATE_FILE` to reprocess all #share notes

